# ci-accepted-red.list -- red CI jobs that do NOT stop main from moving, each held by an OPEN registry row.
#
# Read by scripts/guards/check-push-proven-by-ci.py (pre-push on refs/heads/main). Owner's decision
# 2026-09-30: main moves only to a commit GitHub CI has judged green. A red job listed here is
# accepted ONLY while its registry row (docs/plans/221.1-bug-sweep.md) is open: once the row is
# closed, missing or has no status field, the entry is STALE and the guard refuses every push to
# main until it is removed -- the exemption leaves together with its reason.
#
# Form (one entry per line, `#` at line start = comment):
#   <workflow> / <job name prefix> #NNNN sig:"<cause substring>" [sig:"..." ...] <why>
# <workflow> is the workflow `name:` exactly; the job name is matched by PREFIX, so the long
# parenthesised tail of a job name need not be copied. sig:"..." is the CAUSE SIGNATURE
# (#1662): a substring that must appear in the failed job's log (`gh run view --job <id>
# --log`); several sigs are alternatives, one seen is enough. A red job is accepted ONLY
# when the row is open AND a signature is in the log AND the log carries no marker of a
# different cause (`command not found`, `No such file`, `Traceback`, `panicked` not covered
# by a signature). A signature is taken from a REAL log of a red run of that cause -- never
# invented. Why: 2026-10-02 novac-gate was red for twelve hours by a NEW cause
# (gate-novac.sh called novac_bin_out without sourcing scripts/guards/lib/novac.sh) under
# the name-only acceptance below, and four pushes passed without anyone learning of it.
#
# Not here on purpose: nova-lint and `nova-gate / gate.sh tier push` -- their red (#1355) is
# silenced point-wise in the tree, not accepted.
#
# 2026-10-25, integrator post-092: the #1442 entry was removed -- pre-push
# noticed its signatures no longer match any current red, so the exemption
# was inert; row #1442 stays open in the registry and a NEW red of that
# cause will need fresh signatures from a real log (the form above).
